    "id": "c614b8d1a5c1f6635eb270d1339a7c190511f7e5",
    "message": "Add a reusable development route and My Day cross-workspace replacement\n\nEvery new development question used to need a new selector, parent and\ntree pins, a workflow choice, a jq alternative and a manifest profile,\nabout eleven files and a full local qualification. The new\nv23-dev-batch-no-index-d50 route takes its exact ordered test list from\nthe committed Scripts/v23-dev-batch.json at the dispatched head. The\nfile's digest and list are bound into the dispatched selection,\nadmission rebuilds and compares them, and every listed test must run\nand pass. D50 budgets on GitHub macos-26 only, first attempt only, and\ndevelopment-only: never acceptance, provider or merge credit. Existing\nroutes resolve, admit and record exactly as before.\n\nC57-1 lets a populated cross-workspace My Day Replace project the\ncomplete saved history into the target workspace with remapped\nidentities. Same-workspace Replace stays byte-exact, Clone and Fork\nreject bindings, and the production caller still passes none, so a\npopulated cross-workspace Replace remains fail-closed until the root\nderives bindings. Eleven tests cover history and predecessor\npreservation, every hostile binding, no effect on rejection, and a cold\nreopen.\n\nThe first development batch runs those eleven plus the four C43 signoff\nbaseline methods. Also records the owner's shared-build coverage and\nsignoff decisions, the Phase 1 platform scope and phase ledger, and the\nD2 audit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
